    {
      "id": "bb51d9a4-39c1-4125-8de4-568cd5cf499f",
      "name": "Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1400,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## Webhook Redeliverer\n\nMechanics only; names and windows come from the config key. GitHub never retries a webhook delivery, so on a schedule this lists each active repo's hook that targets the configured ingress path, selects deliveries that failed (non-2xx) inside `redelivery.window_minutes` and were not themselves redeliveries, and asks GitHub to redeliver each exactly once (`<redelivered_prefix><delivery id>`, `redelivery.once_ttl_seconds`). Reconciliation for the event path; the poller and the merge sweep remain the deeper backups."
      }
    },
